# Deployment credentials. examples/anon-share/.env holds TUNNEL_TOKEN, which
# is enough on its own for anyone to run a connector for the tunnel — so this
# rule exists BEFORE the file does, rather than after someone runs `git add -A`
# and rewrites history to take it back.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Ops dashboard for a specific deployment: host addresses, an SSH path, and a
# view of live rooms. Useful locally, not part of the published project, and
# it reads /stats which is deliberately never exposed publicly. Scoped to the
# subdirectory rather than all of tools/ so a genuine repo tool can still land.
/tools/dashboard/
